Q: .NET 10 app can&#39;t load depending dll from subdirectory A: <p>If your goal is clean file structure would recommend publishing as a single file. This is a built-in feature that packs all the dependencies into one file so you don't need a <code>lib</code> folder anymore.</p>
<p>Add this to your <code>.csproj</code> files;</p>
<pre class="lang-xml prettyprint-override"><code>    &lt;PublishSingleFile&gt;true&lt;/PublishSingleFile&gt;
    &lt;SelfContained&gt;true&lt;/SelfContained&gt;
    &lt;RuntimeIdentifier&gt;win-x64&lt;/RuntimeIdentifier&gt;
</code></pre>
<p><a href="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dotnet/core/deploying/single-file/overview?tabs=cli" rel="nofollow noreferrer">https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dotnet/core/deploying/single-file/overview?tabs=cli</a></p>

Q: How do I set Properties for Seq in my appsettings.json file? A: <p>You don't set properties in the seq section specifically. Properties are set in the general Serilog section</p>
<p>Eg.</p>
<pre><code>  &quot;Serilog&quot;: {
    &quot;Using&quot;: [],
    &quot;MinimumLevel&quot;: {
      &quot;Default&quot;: &quot;Information&quot;,
      &quot;Override&quot;: {
        &quot;Microsoft&quot;: &quot;Information&quot;,
        &quot;System&quot;: &quot;Warning&quot;
      }
    },
    &quot;Properties&quot;: {
      &quot;Application&quot;: &quot;MyAppName&quot;
    },
    &quot;Enrich&quot;: [
      &quot;FromLogContext&quot;,
      &quot;WithMachineName&quot;,
      &quot;WithProcessId&quot;,
      &quot;WithTreadId&quot;
    ],
    ...
</code></pre>

