Q: Make fixed map in modified Minesweeper clone A: <p>That code uses the current time to generate a &quot;random&quot; map when the <code>startGame()</code> function is invoked.</p>
<p>Here is the relevant code:</p>
<pre><code>var seed;

//...

function startGame() {
    var d = new Date();
    seed = 2345678901 + (d.getSeconds() * 0xFFFFFF) + (d.getMinutes() * 0xFFFF);
    // ...
</code></pre>
<p>Using the current time like this makes the code &quot;non-deterministic&quot;, i.e. you can get different results when the code is run at different times.</p>
<p>To generate the same map every time you can hard-code the global <code>seed</code> variable once instead of generating a new seed whenever <code>startGame()</code> is invoked.</p>
<p>Here is an example - I've just manually evaluated the current seconds and minutes and replaced the <code>d.getSeconds()</code> and <code>d.getMinutes()</code> calls with constant values (ala xkcd: <a href="https://xkcd.com/221/" rel="nofollow noreferrer">https://xkcd.com/221/</a>):</p>
<pre><code>// Hard-code the seed
var seed = 2345678901 + (9 * 0xFFFFFF) + (31 * 0xFFFF);

//...

function startGame() {
    /*
    // And remove these lines so the seed won't change:
    ~~var d = new Date();~~
    ~~seed = 2345678901 + (d.getSeconds() * 0xFFFFFF) + (d.getMinutes() * 0xFFFF);~~
    */
    // ...
</code></pre>
